<title>USA: Midwest Cash Grain PM - Slow sales support basis - May 15.</title>
<headline>Midwest Cash Grain PM - Slow sales support basis - May 15.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Corn and soybean basis bids continued to find support Thursday from slow farmer selling in U.S. Midwest cash grain markets, dealers said.</p>
<p>Where weather allowed, farmers continued to plant both corn and soybeans.</p>
<p>Farmers in the eastern Corn Belt, where conditions have been too cool and wet to plant, were eyeing forecasts that show more much warmer weather for the weekend.</p>
<p>&quot;There are stil pockets where it's too wet to work, but if the weather holds, they'll (farmers) be back in by the beginning of next week,&quot; said an Ohio dealer.</p>
<p>Corn basis in Kansas City cash markets jumped as much as four cents per bushel in response to tight supplies and a sudden increase in demand for corn for spot delivery, dealers there said.  </p>
<p>Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures, cash $/bu.</p>
